Dear colleagues,

Please be advised that QSCP-MOC-2014-017 has been fully implemented within ATU-100. The DEA strength has been increased from 25 to 30 wt% to accommodate the required higher sour-gas throughput.

QSCP-HAM-OPS and QSCP-HAM-INSP should update all relevant monitoring records to reflect this change in operating conditions. Inspection intervals for rich amine and regenerator overhead circuits remain subject to the 3-year thickness interval requirement as per site protocols.

Regards,  Robert Hendricks Unit Engineer ATU-100, P.Eng. QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department

